---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SELLER, LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED } from '../data/shop.js';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | gazza.ltd"
  description="How gazza.ltd handles your data: what the calculators don't collect, what we keep when you buy something, advertising cookies, and your rights."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">Last updated {LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED}.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Every calculator and tool on this site runs entirely in your
        browser. Whatever you type into a calculator, word-game field, or
        text tool is processed on your device and is never sent to, or
        stored on, our servers. We don't ask you to sign up, and we don't
        collect the numbers, letters or text you enter.
      </p>
      <p>
        The one exception is buying something. If you buy the MTD Income Tax
        Readiness Tracker, we need your name, email address and order details
        to take payment and send you the file. That's explained under
        "If you buy from us" below.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site does use cookies for advertising and, once ads are
        enabled, third-party vendors including Google may use cookies to
        serve and measure ads. That's covered in detail below.
      </p>

      <h2>If you buy from us</h2>
      <p>
        {SELLER.name} (company number {SELLER.companyNumber}, registered office
        {' '}{SELLER.registeredOffice}) is the data controller for purchases.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Payment — Stripe.</strong> Checkout runs on Stripe. Stripe collects
          your card details, name, email address and billing country, and we never see
          your full card number. Stripe processes this under its
          {' '}<a href="https://stripe.com/gb/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
          Stripe shares your name, email, country, the amount paid and an order
          reference with us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Delivery — Cloudflare.</strong> To give you a download link we store
          your order reference, your email address and a download counter on
          Cloudflare. That delivery record is deleted automatically after 72 hours.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email — Resend.</strong> We send your download link and order
          confirmation using Resend, an email delivery service, which processes your
          email address and the message under its
          {' '}<a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
          Some of these providers are based in the USA; transfers are covered by
          the UK–US data bridge or standard contractual clauses.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Why:</strong> to perform our contract with you (taking payment,
        delivering the file, refunds and support) and to meet legal obligations
        (tax and accounting records). We don't use your purchase details for
        marketing and we don't sell them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>How long:</strong> order records in Stripe are kept for six years
        after the end of the financial year of the sale, because UK company and tax
        law requires it. Delivery records are deleted after 72 hours.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Your rights:</strong> you can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to
        correct or delete it (where we're not required to keep it), or object to how
        we use it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SELLER.email}`}>{SELLER.email}</a>.
        If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data you can complain to the
        {' '}<a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We work with Google AdSense (or, at higher traffic, similar ad
        networks) to display ads that help keep every tool on this site
        free. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve
        ads based on your prior visits to this site and other sites on the
        internet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to
        serve ads based on your visits to this site and other sites. You can
        opt out of personalised advertising by visiting Google's
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Ads Settings
        </a>, or opt out of a range of third-party vendors' use of cookies
        for personalised advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          aboutads.info
        </a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Other third-party ad networks we work with may also place cookies
        on your device to serve and measure ads. Where that's the case,
        we'll name the vendor here and link to their own opt-out options.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use privacy-friendly, aggregate analytics to understand which
        pages get used and roughly how much traffic the site gets. This
        does not use cookies to track you individually across other sites,
        and doesn't identify you personally.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may process
        standard technical information (such as your IP address) as part
        of delivering the site to you and protecting it from abuse, as
        described in
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Cloudflare's own privacy policy
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can control cookies through your browser settings, including
        blocking or deleting them. Doing so may affect how ads are shown to
        you but won't stop any calculator on this site from working, since
        none of them depend on cookies to function.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SELLER.email}`}>{SELLER.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes — for example when a new ad network or
        analytics tool is added — this page will be updated and the date at
        the top will change accordingly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
